+\paragraph{\revredreplace{Graph legal analysis and calibration.}{Graph retrieval and evidence selection.}}
+\revredreplace{Network analysis has been used for statutory cross-references (\mbox{\citealp{boulet2021measuring}}), contract graph extraction is active (\mbox{\citealp{dechtiar2025graphgrpolex}}), and conformal ideas inspire calibrated evidence signals (\mbox{\citealp{vovk2005algorithmic}}; \mbox{\citealp{gibbs2021adaptive}}).  \samcgs{} is complementary because it assumes a record graph and focuses on risk search inside cyclic components.}{GraphRAG uses entity graphs and community summaries for query-focused summarization \citep{edge2024graphrag}. ToG-2 couples knowledge-graph traversal with document retrieval \citep{ma2025tog2}, and G-Retriever selects query-relevant subgraphs through prize-collecting Steiner tree optimization \citep{he2024gretriever}. Our task centers on retaining risk endpoints in a compact output subgraph; \samcgs{} accumulates relation-level evidence during local search within an \scc{}.}
 
